  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pressure-cooker minestrone takes about 20 minutes. The pressure builds a richness that takes an hour on the stovetop. The vegetables soften fully into the tomato base. The beans absorb the surrounding flavour rather than sitting apart in the broth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use what is in season and in the fridge. Minestrone is truly flexible, courgette, green beans, leek, spinach, cavolo nero, or butternut squash all work in addition to or instead of any of the vegetables listed here."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pasta is traditional. Cook it separately and stir it in at serving. Pasta left in stored soup absorbs liquid and turns mushy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
